1
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,797
The sun's setting? Already?

2
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,820
It can't be. Guys!

3
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,062
He really was telling the truth!

4
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:24,920
The priest's new ability!

5
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,017
He already had it back on the shuttle!

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,865
And now everything is
moving at a faster speed!

7
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:32,117
Everything in this world is...

8
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,257
And I don't just mean the machines.

9
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,281
I'm talking literally everything.

10
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,876
Oh shit, the sun's already gone down.

11
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:41,840
Does that mean the
completion of his ability?

12
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:45,920
Where is he?

13
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,709
Where did that bastard go?

14
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:51,397
The longest I can stop time
is five seconds at most.

15
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,797
I have to locate him and strike him down.

16
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,762
All in the span of five seconds.

17
00:00:56,540 --> 00:00:57,540
That's the limit.

18
00:00:57,860 --> 00:00:59,180
Now time will resume.

19
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:01,110
What?

20
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:02,260
It can't be!

21
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:04,109
He's using it as a spring!

22
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:27,457
I will make this clear once and for all.

23
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:29,840
Time will keep racing by.

24
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:32,648
But for your clarification?

25
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:36,537
I did not obtain this ability just
so I could dispose of you all!

26
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:39,208
nor did I do it to
become the most powerful.

27
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:44,617
The true purpose of this ability
is to guide the masses of humanity.

28
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,465
towards everlasting happiness.

29
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:51,100
Allow me to introduce you to my
new stand, my gift to humanity.

30
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:54,357
I shall christen my stand...

31
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,220
Made in Heaven!

32
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:21,980
Itaami wo nori Cairo tabi

33
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:25,757
Kokoro wa eilu

34
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:30,860
ni togisuma sareru

35
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:36,457
Cairo kai Zero Chaka

36
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:39,760
mei no sai hate de

37
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,557
I'll

38
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,957
see

39
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:09,040
you

40
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:10,510
next time.

41
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:34,879
The reason for my disposing of you
all is for the future of humanity.

42
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,357
Your deaths here are nothing personal.

43
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:42,820
For the sake of all mankind's happiness,
you shall become necessary sacrifices.

44
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:47,100
Ghost gun! Fire!

45
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,820
It's no use, Emporio!

46
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,437
Bullets aren't gonna hit him!

47
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:53,600
Nuh-uh, Jolene!

48
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:56,377
I aim for the wall of
the next building over!

49
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:59,017
And I must put one of her
stickers on the bullet!

50
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,571
Thanks to that, there are two bullets now!

51
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:04,410
Emporio...

52
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:06,780
He's coming back around!

53
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,969
Hold on tightly, everyone!

54
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:12,296
No matter what happens, we
can't let go of each other!

55
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:28,940
Crap, it's him!

56
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,160
He's chasing us!

57
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:33,791
Because smack is a stand, its
movements aren't accelerated!

58
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,497
But he's on our asses!

59
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:36,520
Emporio!

60
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:40,077
Put a sticker on another one of
your bullets and shoot again!

61
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:42,977
We're gonna make our way to
the wetlands just like this!

62
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,413
Head towards the ocean!

63
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:49,324
If we're surrounded by water, there's one
way we can kill this psycho time wizard!

64
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:53,460
The priest already caught up to us!

65
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,993
He's gonna wait for us at that building!

66
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:59,557
Use this next bullet to change
our trajectory, Emporio!

67
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:00,660
To the ocean!

68
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,628
That's where we need to be!

69
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:07,408
Focus on the marshes and aim the bullet
at the rocks jutting out of the water!

70
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:16,540
He's coming this way!

71
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:18,520
He's too fast! Listen,

72
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:22,917
even if the priest is able to pursue us
through this state of accelerated time,

73
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,500
he only has one stand.

74
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:28,687
Also, I'm willing to bet that
its power is only above average.

75
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:33,524
He has no other choice but to pick
each of us off, one at a time.

76
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:36,657
That's when we have the
chance to beat him down.

77
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:40,620
At the exact moment when he tries
to come in and end my life, Mr.

78
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:43,557
Jotaro, that's when I'm
going to give you a signal.

79
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:47,993
When I do, stop time immediately and
kill that fucker before he gets away.

80
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,617
As for the timing,

81
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:51,597
you're going to want to
stop time at precisely

82
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:54,386
the same instant that
his attack hits my body.

83
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:56,620
Do you hear me?

84
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,117
Don't stop it any earlier than that.

85
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:00,040
Do it after.

86
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:02,498
This is all going to happen quickly.

87
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,032
The timing is important.

88
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:06,737
You'll have to grab him
while he's in mid-attack.

89
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:09,526
And to do that, your
Star Platinum is the key.

90
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:11,980
Yo, wait a second.

91
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:13,319
You're doing what?

92
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:15,200
I don't understand.

93
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,148
What are you trying to say?

94
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:19,380
Anastasia, that's a good idea.

95
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:24,137
But although Poochie said he'll end you
first, he might not act on his words.

96
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:25,867
We can't trust what he says.

97
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:31,640
Thinking about it a bit more
logically, you'll end me first. No.

98
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:35,177
I get why you might think
that, but it isn't accurate.

99
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:38,797
My Diver Drive is already in your
body, protecting you like before.

100
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,340
And it's not just you.

101
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,960
Jolene, Emporio, and Ermes too.

102
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:44,200
You're all safe.

103
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:47,157
As long as you stay within
an arm's length of me.

104
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:50,064
So no matter who ends up
getting attacked first,

105
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:54,605
the brunt of that first blow will
be absorbed by my Diver Drive.

106
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:57,897
After that you'll feel
a sensation through your

107
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:00,277
body that's gonna be the
signal from my stand!

108
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:03,717
That it's go time we
clear that's how it has to

109
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,980
be time can't stop until
after his attack lands!

110
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:09,977
Anastasia are you going for a draw?

111
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:12,637
What no way are you out of your mind?

112
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:16,997
His next attack will definitely
kill you most likely but maybe

113
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:20,677
before he strikes my vitals I can
manage to send the signal off!

114
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:24,897
I have been having good luck
recently haven't I Emporio?

115
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:28,377
Since I broke out of prison
I've managed not to die somehow!

116
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:31,297
If I can just keep on
living when this shitstorm

117
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:34,204
is over I'm finally gonna
ask Jolene to marry me

118
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:39,117
or something like that! You know?

119
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,920
Sure!

120
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:46,837
Go ahead.

121
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:47,920
Just propose.

122
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:52,707
I'm not saying this because I'm
in despair over our situation.

123
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:55,371
There's still some hope left in your plan.

124
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,480
It's not dark at all.

125
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,200
There might be only one path, but
if there's even a sliver of hope,

126
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:04,958
then that'll be the path to success.

127
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,757
He's over there!

128
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:14,600
He's already on the rock
ahead of us! Emporio!

129
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:21,300
Everybody, gather up!

130
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,860
Get closer to me, now!

131
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:26,370
There!

132
00:08:26,453 --> 00:08:28,242
He's coming around to the right!

133
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,510
He's here!

134
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,020
I see.

135
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,740
Due to the splashes,

136
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:37,197
being surrounded by water makes it
easier to see which way he's going.

137
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:39,320
Not yet, Mr. Jotaro.

138
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,896
Whatever you do, don't stop time yet.

139
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,904
If he gets away, it's all over.

140
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:47,066
Capturing him is the
only way we can win this.

141
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,886
You've got to sense the
signal with your body.

142
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,720
Hey, wait a second. Look up.

143
00:08:57,980 --> 00:08:59,757
What's wrong with all the clouds?

144
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,722
They're racing by at insane
speeds like a rocket.

145
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,520
and what the heck is going on?

146
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:07,917
The sky to the east is getting brighter.

147
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:08,900
What the hell?

148
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:12,557
Seriously, aren't they
moving way too fast?

149
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:15,057
An hour was supposed to feel
like two to three minutes,

150
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:17,597
which means it should have
taken at least 20 to 30 minutes?

151
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:19,209
for the sun to rise again.

152
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,040
It doesn't make sense.

153
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:24,222
The sun is coming up at
an impossibly high speed.

154
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,197
Hey, what the hell does that mean?

155
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:34,574
Isn't that time is starting
to accelerate even more now?

156
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:38,957
Birds all over the world are still
flying at their natural speed.

157
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:41,216
So are butterflies and other insects.

158
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,350
Also,

159
00:09:42,433 --> 00:09:44,317
there are no reported
cases of flowers or plants

160
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:47,400
blooming abruptly or
withering away at rapid rates.

161
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:48,722
See this glass?

162
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:51,117
I'm currently holding it in my hand.

163
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:55,847
As long as it remains in my grasp, nothing
happens even if I shake or swirl it.

164
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:59,100
However, once I remove
my grip from the glass...

165
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:00,610
You see?

166
00:10:00,693 --> 00:10:02,317
We can't even see it fall.

167
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:05,577
It's already broken on the
floor before you realize.

168
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:08,137
It the only possible explanation for this

169
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:10,937
phenomenon is that time
is Accelerating everything

170
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:12,757
in the world is
progressively getting faster

171
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:14,877
except for The movements
of living organisms.

172
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:18,417
This is all my assistance fault.

173
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:20,577
I'm the Number one monthly manga artist.

174
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:25,257
Yeah there's no way that I could have
only Drawn one page in the entire night.

175
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:26,399
It's not possible.

176
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:29,340
Oh, what?

177
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:33,477
And for some reason, the ink on the pen
dries before it even touches the paper.

178
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,180
What am I supposed to do?

179
00:10:38,260 --> 00:10:40,040
Yes, what is it? What?

180
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:42,946
There's a manga artist
that's still got it in?

181
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,520
And who could that be?

182
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,366
What kind of person are they?

183
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:48,020
Rohan Kishibe.

184
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:51,860
The tide's going too fast.

185
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:53,717
I can't see the movement of the waves.

186
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,877
We can't read where the
priest is going like this.

187
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:56,790
Shit!

188
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,724
Where is he going to come from?

189
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,680
Everyone get ready!

190
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,340
Stone Ocean!

191
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:06,130
Smack!

192
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:07,830
Mr.

193
00:11:07,913 --> 00:11:09,360
Jotaro, not just yet.

194
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:10,638
We're almost there.

195
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:12,507
Wait for the signal to come.

196
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:22,620
Do it now! Stop time!
Stop platinum! The world!

197
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:28,360
I got you!

198
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,680
Take this, Father Pochi!

199
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:37,650
What?!

200
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,489
He used Jolene's stand
to attack Anastasia!

201
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:42,640
He's a step ahead of us!

202
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,940
Only four more seconds.

203
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:51,755
If I'm not able to finish him off now,

204
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:54,781
I'll just hide within the
accelerating time again.

205
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,569
As soon as time resumes,
we'll be done for!

206
00:11:58,100 --> 00:12:01,806
I have to go at him with everything
I've got while I still can!

207
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,580
Three more seconds!

208
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:05,440
Two seconds!

209
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:24,050
Knives!

210
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:27,717
While he was falling, the priest had
already thrown them into the air,

211
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:29,800
just like how Dio did in the past.

212
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:46,000
Oh my, it seems you
were late by two steps.

213
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:03,820
The Joestar bloodline has to be expected.

214
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:07,104
They drew strength from
their pride and courage,

215
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,680
and came together to conquer their fate.

216
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:14,020
However, that connection through
blood is also their weakness.

217
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:18,620
Jotaro Kujo, your greatest
weakness is your daughter.

218
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:22,177
Push - push - push - Push -

219
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:29,260
push

220
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:38,750
- Hey,

221
00:13:38,833 --> 00:13:39,663
old man.

222
00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:41,600
Don't leave.

223
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,320
I did steal a car.

224
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:48,320
I was leaving school.

225
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:54,240
In the supermarket parking
lot, there was a car.

226
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,220
Why did I do something like that?

227
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:02,980
But I know Dad's gonna come save me.

228
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,120
He'll be here.

229
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:06,540
Definitely.

230
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:09,780
Dad'll be here soon.

231
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,060
To save me.

232
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:31,700
I must eliminate any obstacles
in the way of my destiny.

233
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:36,660
I feel no remorse for them or
you, nor will I let you go free.

234
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,880
I'll put an end to everything.

235
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:43,900
But to you, young Emporio, I'm the
one who killed your mother, aren't I?

236
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:57,800
Shoot me then, pull the trigger so you can
leave this godforsaken world as a martyr.

237
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:03,273
This is where your fate comes to an end!

238
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,050
Emporia!

239
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:21,540
Jolene Kujo!

240
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,210
Showstar!

241
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:38,857
Do you truly think you can get away?

242
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:40,637
The speed at which you swim through water

243
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:43,249
is slower than if you
were running on land!

244
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:51,370
Jolene!

245
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:54,000
I caught a dolphin with Stone Ocean.

246
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:56,620
No matter how fast time is going,

247
00:15:57,040 --> 00:16:00,157
every living creature is
moving at its natural speed.

248
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:02,358
And then there's you, Father Poochy.

249
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:06,577
With your speed, you could probably
catch up to this dolphin easily.

250
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:08,366
But distance is what matters.

251
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:10,560
You can reach us at close range.

252
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:13,702
But how many meters can
you keep on swimming for?

253
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:15,260
500 meters?

254
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:16,900
Maybe even 800?

255
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,550
A hundred?

256
00:16:18,633 --> 00:16:19,463
How long can you last?

257
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:22,817
Can you swim longer distances than
a dolphin without getting tired?

258
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:25,057
That has nothing to do
with the flow of time.

259
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:28,297
It's still the same distance whether
you're picking something up or swimming.

260
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:30,380
That doesn't change. And plus,

261
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:34,217
it has to be at a distance where you
can swim back to shore without drowning.

262
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,160
I won't ever let you get away.

263
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:38,960
This tiresome feud between us ends now.

264
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:42,736
I can't have any trace of
your existence in my future.

265
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,817
Chulene, climb the rope.

266
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,841
Hurry up and come to the dolphin!

267
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:53,214
Emporio, because of Anastasia's
sacrificing himself to protect my father,

268
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:56,060
I'm still alive, but
that's the only reason.

269
00:16:57,340 --> 00:17:00,457
And thanks to Ermes buying
time attacking the priest,

270
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:03,540
I was able to extend my
rope to catch this dolphin.

271
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,117
When dolphins let people
ride on their back,

272
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:09,457
I heard that they swim in a way
that their rider won't ever drown.

273
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:10,780
Hurry! Hurry!

274
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:12,885
Get over here already, Jolene!

275
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:14,980
Your rope is unraveling even more!

276
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:18,437
I know without a doubt
that Dolphin is going

277
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:21,226
to carry you somewhere
safe and out of danger.

278
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,560
What are you saying? Hurry!

279
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,821
You can still make it over to me!

280
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:28,080
Emporium, I can't go with you.

281
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:32,537
Wherever I go, the Priest will sense the
presence of the Joestar blood within me.

282
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:35,417
And no matter how far I
run, I'll sense him too.

283
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,382
He'll keep following me forever.

284
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:42,266
If I stay here, you won't
be able to get away.

285
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:46,740
Everything will be okay, Emporio.

286
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:49,717
You'll be going the rest
of the way yourself.

287
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:50,960
You can do this.

288
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:53,813
I have total faith in your capabilities.

289
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:58,314
The ones who died so that you could
live are Anastasia, our friend Ermes,

290
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,840
and my father,

291
00:18:01,300 --> 00:18:02,420
Jotaro Keicho.

292
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:04,880
Keep on living.

293
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,400
Your only hope!

294
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:09,877
I don't know what the heck
you're even talking about!

295
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,540
No! Please don't go!

296
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:17,380
Just wait! Hold on! Jolyne!
Stop! Don't leave me!

297
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:20,487
Hurry and pull yourself
off the rope already!

298
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,520
He's getting worn out.

299
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,314
I'll hold him off for as long as I can!

300
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:34,440
Bring it, Father Poochie!

301
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:38,820
Stone Ocean!

302
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:47,690
No!

303
00:18:48,220 --> 00:18:49,050
July!

304
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,800
Whoa, hey, what's that?

305
00:18:54,060 --> 00:18:56,260
Is that the sun rising? No way!

306
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:58,437
The sun's coming up again already?

307
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:00,837
It doesn't even look
like a sphere anymore!

308
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:03,038
It's more like a long belt of light!

309
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:06,240
The hands on my watch disappeared! No!

310
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:09,917
They're just going way too fast
for me to see with the naked eye!

311
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,837
The day's over! It's over!

312
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:12,940
Now it's morning!

313
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,101
And night again!

314
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,900
This is crazy!

315
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:18,660
Time is accelerating even more!

316
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:21,450
Shit!

317
00:19:21,533 --> 00:19:22,498
This is really bad!

318
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:23,980
Get the canned food!

319
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:26,877
All the raw meat's gonna rot
and we can't eat it anymore!

320
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:27,790
Buy it out!

321
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,567
Buy out all the canned food!

322
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:31,427
We're gonna run out of food!

323
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:34,137
Look at all this window dust collecting!

324
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:35,455
The frame is rotting!

325
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:53,160
Whoa, my teeth!

326
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:56,325
The implants I just got
put in are falling out!

327
00:19:58,700 --> 00:19:59,900
What the hell, man?

328
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:01,356
What's with the sky?

329
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:03,157
Where the fuck did the sun go?

330
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:05,917
Is that strip of light in the
sky supposed to be the sun?

331
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,920
Is the time noon or is it night?

332
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,417
What day of the week is it?

333
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,837
And for that matter, what's even the year?

334
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:13,861
It's starting to get really cold.

335
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:15,686
The climate is changing, too.

336
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:20,860
What's going on?

337
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:23,997
The rocks are changing
shape because of the waves.

338
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:26,374
Is time ever going to stop speeding up?

339
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:28,380
How much more?

340
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:31,484
How much longer is this
nightmare going to last?

341
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:48,040
Now even the terrain is changing too!

342
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:58,640
What in the world is this? How bizarre!

343
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,412
It's only living things!

344
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:10,460
I can't breathe!

345
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:40,457
What in God's name are you doing
in here without any clothes on?

346
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:41,500
Huh?

347
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:42,977
What the... I...

348
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:44,600
Shut up and stop stalling!

349
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:47,057
You and the prisoners need to get dressed!

350
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,980
But why am I naked too, though?

351
00:21:49,260 --> 00:21:50,760
I mean, what happened?

352
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:53,237
Time was going all fast, and then...

353
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:54,261
This ain't good!

354
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,437
I'm naked on camera!

355
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,814
They'll misunderstand!

356
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:00,580
Is this...

357
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,540
This place is...

358
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:05,200
I've been here!

359
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,520
I know it!

360
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:11,257
This place is Green Dolphin
Street State Prison.

361
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:14,800
And I'm in the hallway in
front of the visiting room.

362
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:30,180
Although you think I cope!

363
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:35,060
My head is filled with hope.

364
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:40,117
Of some place

365
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:43,800
other than here.

366
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:50,200
Although you think I smile!

367
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:55,280
Inside and all the while

368
00:22:57,060 --> 00:23:03,460
I'm wondering about my destiny?

369
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,917
I'm thinking

370
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:13,597
about all the

371
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:18,497
things I'd like

372
00:23:18,580 --> 00:23:24,500
to do in my life.

373
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:29,277
I'm a dreamer.

374
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:34,440
A distant dreamer.

375
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:39,420
Dreaming far away.

376
00:23:41,780 --> 00:23:44,580
From today!

377
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:55,330
Thank you.

378
00:24:24,500 --> 00:24:25,330
Thank you.
